    "prompt": "Eye-level view standing on top of the whale skeleton spine, looking back along it toward the tail: the walkway is the flat tops of the vertebrae, three blocks wide, each vertebra a squared drum with a tall bone blade rising from its middle, gaps between vertebrae; on both sides the tops of the ribs curve down out of sight into the cloud sea far below; the spine dwindles into the distance toward the tail.",
    "style_note": "Whale-fall (鲸落), in the same hand throughout: a Minecraft-style voxel world rendered as clean, softly lit concept art; the subject is the bleached skeleton of a colossal dead sky-whale floating motionless above an endless sea of white clouds, under a pale high sky. Bone is chalk-white to warm ivory, built of large square blocks so its stepped edges read as voxel masonry; small ruined grey-stone temple pieces sit inside the skull. Calm, eerie, vast; no creatures, no people, no text. Each image is ONE single full-frame view of that place, filling the frame edge to edge: never a sheet, never a grid, never a panel, never an inset or a caption.",
